Context('Numeric');
$a = 0;
$b = pi;
$err = 0.0001;
$Mt = 1;
$Ms = 1;
$nt = sqrt(($b-$a)**3*$Mt/(12*$err));
$nt = int($nt + 0.5);
$ns = (($b-$a)**5*$Ms/(180*$err))**(1./4);
$ns = int($ns + .99999);
if ($ns%2==1) {     
  $ns++;
}

############################################################
# Body
############################################################

BEGIN_PGML
Find [`n`] such that the error in approximating the given definite integral is less than [`0.0001`] when using the Trapezoidal Rule and Simpson's Rule.

For the integral [`\int_{0}^{\pi} \sin(x) \, dx\text{:}`]

END_PGML

